{title: Create in Me a Clean Heart}
{subtitle: Psalms 51:12–14}
{key: F}
{tempo: 69}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Am/C] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Against you, you a[F]lone, have I [C]sinned
And my [Dm7]sin is always there before me a[Bb]gain
I [F]have done what is evil in [C]your sight, I know
Have [Dm]mercy on me, O God, and [Bb]do not let me go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Create in [F]me a clean heart, [C]O God
And [Dm7]renew a steadfast spirit with[Bb]in me
Do not [F]cast me from your pre[C]sence
And [Dm7]do not take your [C]holy Spirit from [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Cleanse me with His [F]Son, and I will be [C]clean
Wash me, [Dm7]and I will be whiter than snow [Bb]
The bones that [F]you have broken, [C]let them sing
[Dm]Let me hear the joy and [Bb]gladness that you bring
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Create in [F]me a clean heart, [C]O God
And re[Dm7]new a steadfast spirit within [Bb]me
Do not [F]cast me from your pre[C]sence
And [Dm]do not take your [C]holy Spirit from [Bb]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Re[Dm]store to me the joy of your salva[Bb]tion
And sus[F]tain me with a will[C]ing spirit
A [Dm]broken and crushed heart, O [Bb]God, you will not de[C]spair
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Christ, created [F]me, a clean heart, [C]O God [Dm][Bb]
Created [F]me, a clean [C]heart
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
